# SYNTAX TEST "text.html.tiddlywiki5.memetic-wikitext" "A sigil's verb reads only inside a call"

# A sigil is a call TiddlyWiki builds, so its verb reads only where the base reads a call. Text that
# merely LOOKS like `<<~ set …>>` inside a comment, a raw fence or a typed block builds no call, and
# the verb there reads as the comment or the raw text it stands in.

<!-- <<~ set hud="x">> -->
#        ^^^ comment.block.html.tiddlywiki5
#        ^^^ - keyword.control.sigil.memetic-wikitext

```
<<~ set hud="x">>
#   ^^^ markup.inline.raw
#   ^^^ - keyword.control.sigil.memetic-wikitext
```

$$$text/plain
<<~ set hud="x">>
#   ^^^ markup.inline.raw
#   ^^^ - keyword.control.sigil.memetic-wikitext
$$$

# CONTROL: the sigil itself names its verb.
<<~ set hud="x">>
#   ^^^ keyword.control.sigil.memetic-wikitext
#   ^^^ entity.name.function.sigil.memetic-wikitext

<<~/ahu>>
#  ^ punctuation.definition.sigil.close.memetic-wikitext
